Before implementing any Sakshi SDK integration, first study the SDK documentation completely.

Read these documents in order:

1. https://github.com/RajnishKMehta/Sakshi-SDK/blob/main/README.md
2. temp-docs/sakshi-sdk_api_usage.adoc (local file)
3. https://github.com/RajnishKMehta/Sakshi-SDK/blob/main/docs/architecture.adoc
4. https://github.com/RajnishKMehta/Sakshi-SDK/blob/main/docs/ipc_specification.adoc (optional reference if needed)

Do not start implementation until you fully understand how the SDK works.

To avoid repeatedly searching through the documentation, create concise reference notes inside the `temp-docs/` directory containing only the important APIs, workflows, callbacks, request/response models, and integration details that will be useful during development.

Use those notes as your temporary reference while implementing the project.

----------------------------

After understanding the SDK, begin integrating it into Sakshi Camera.

Implement the integration cleanly using modern Android best practices.

Follow the SDK documentation exactly wherever applicable.

--------------
Default Camera Settings
--------------

Update the default camera preferences:

- Camera Sounds: OFF
- Zero Shutter Lag: ON
- Image Quality: 100%
- Remove EXIF after capture: OFF

--------------
Vault Integration
--------------

Default Vault package:

rajnishkmehta.sakshi.vault

When the Camera application starts:

1. Determine the currently configured Vault package.
2. Use the Sakshi SDK to send a Vault Ping request.
3. Validate the response using `VaultPingResponse`.

If the Vault responds successfully:

- Continue normally.

If no compatible Vault responds:

- Show a user-friendly dialog explaining that the configured Vault application is unavailable.
- Allow the user to select another installed application.
- Verify the selected application using the SDK ping before accepting it.
- If validation succeeds, save it as the new Vault application.
- If validation fails, display an error and ask the user to choose another application.

The dialog should also include a secondary action:

"If you don't have a compatible Vault installed, download the official Sakshi Vault."

Download URL:

https://github.com/RajnishKMehta/Sakshi-Vault/releases/latest/download/app-release.apk

The currently selected Vault application must also be configurable later from the Camera settings screen.

--------------
SDK Events
--------------

Implement handling for all important SDK callbacks and errors.

For `CopyDoneAck`:

- Receive the callback correctly.
- Add a clear TODO indicating that the post-copy behavior will be implemented later.
- Do not implement that functionality yet.

Implement proper error handling for every SDK interaction.

--------------
Implementation Quality
--------------

Keep the integration:

- Clean
- Modular
- Well documented
- Maintainable
- Consistent with the existing project architecture

If you discover any limitation, missing SDK API, or documentation issue during integration, document it before implementing workarounds.

Only begin coding after the documentation has been fully understood.
